{:edb/db-before-t 1248 :edb/db-after-t 1249 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534561 50 #inst "2026-10-08T00:58:42.891Z" 13194139534561 true] [17592186063865 1100 "Find the value of $f(x) = \\dfrac{e^{\\left\\lfloor x+2 \\right\\rfloor}}{2x+1}$ at $x = 0.75$. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534561 false] [17592186063865 1100 "Find the value of $f(x) = \\dfrac{e^{\\left\\lfloor x+2 \\right\\rfloor}}{2x+1}$ at $x = 0.75.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534561 true] [17592186063865 1145 "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad  n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 0.75,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊0.75+2⌋}}{2(0.75)+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\lfloor 2.75\\right\\rfloor = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =\\frac{{e}^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2.5} \\\\  & =2.955\\,62… \\\\  & ≈2.96,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534561 true] [17592186063865 1145 "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad n \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 0.75$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0.75) &= (e^{⌊0.75 + 2⌋})/(2(0.75) + 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\lfloor 2.75\\right\\rfloor = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0.75) &= \\frac{e^{⌊2.75⌋}}{2.5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{2}}{2.5} \\\\\n&= 2.95562… \\\\\n&\\approx 2.96\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534561 false] [17592186063866 1100 "Find the value of $f(x) = \\left \\lceil e^{6x-5} \\right \\rceil$ at $x = 1.25$." 13194139534561 false] [17592186063866 1100 "Find the value of $f(x) = \\left \\lceil e^{6x-5} \\right \\rceil$ at $x = 1.25.$" 13194139534561 true] [17592186063866 1145 "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad n-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 1.25$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1.25) &= ⌈e^{6(1.25) - 5}⌉ \\\\\n&= ⌈e^{7.5 - 5}⌉ \\\\\n&= ⌈e^{2.5}⌉\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left \\lceil e^{2.5} \\right \\rceil = \\left \\lceil 12.182\\,49 \\ldots \\right \\rceil = 13\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1.25) &= ⌈e^{2.5}⌉ \\\\\n&= 13\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534561 false] [17592186063866 1145 "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 1.25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.25) & =⌈{e}^{6(1.25)-5}⌉ \\\\  & =⌈{e}^{7.5-5}⌉ \\\\  & =⌈{e}^{2.5}⌉.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left \\lceil e^{2.5} \\right \\rceil = \\left \\lceil 12.182\\,49 \\ldots \\right \\rceil = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.25) & =⌈{e}^{2.5}⌉ \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534561 true] [17592186064025 1100 "If $f(x)=2x+\\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{x}{5} \\right\\rfloor$, then what is the value of $f(-0.5)$?" 13194139534561 false] [17592186064025 1100 "If $f(x)=2x+\\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{x}{5} \\right\\rfloor,$ then what is the value of $f(-0.5)?$" 13194139534561 true] [17592186064025 1145 "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad  n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-0.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.5) & =2\\cdot (-0.5)+⌊\\frac{-0.5}{5}⌋ \\\\  & =-1+⌊-0.1⌋.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-0.1⌋=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.5) & =-1+⌊-0.1⌋ \\\\  & =-1+(-1) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534561 true] [17592186064025 1145 "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad n \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-0.5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-0.5) &= 2 \\cdot (-0.5) + ⌊\\frac{-0.5}{5}⌋ \\\\\n&=-1 + ⌊ - 0.1⌋\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function we have\n\n$$\n⌊ - 0.1⌋ =-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-0.5) &= -1 + ⌊ - 0.1⌋ \\\\\n&=-1 + (-1) \\\\\n&=-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534561 false] [17592186064026 1100 "Find the value of $f(x)=(\\lceil 6x-3 \\rceil -2)^3$ at $x=0.4$." 13194139534561 false] [17592186064026 1100 "Find the value of $f(x)=(\\lceil 6x-3 \\rceil -2)^3$ at $x=0.4.$" 13194139534561 true] [17592186064026 1145 "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad n-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0.4) &= (⌈6(0.4) - 3⌉ - 2)^{3} \\\\\n&= (⌈2.4 - 3⌉ - 2)^{3} \\\\\n&= (⌈ - 0.6⌉ - 2)^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\lceil -0.6 \\rceil = 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0.4) &= (⌈ - 0.6⌉ - 2)^{3} \\\\\n&= (0 - 2)^{3} \\\\\n&= (-2)^{3} \\\\\n&=-8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534561 false] [17592186064026 1145 "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\\lceil x \\rceil$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\lceil x \\rceil = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn-1 \\lt x \\leq n, \\quad n\\in\\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.4) & =(⌈6(0.4)-3⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(⌈2.4-3⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(⌈-0.6⌉-2)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\lceil -0.6 \\rceil = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.4) & =(⌈-0.6⌉-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(0-2)^{3} \\\\  & =(-2)^{3} \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534561 true] [17592186064111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295431 13194139534561 true] [17592186064111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295434 13194139534561 true] [17592186064111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295437 13194139534561 true] [17592186064111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295440 13194139534561 true] [17592186064111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295444 13194139534561 true] [17592186064112 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295465 13194139534561 true] [17592186064112 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295472 13194139534561 true] [17592186064112 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295514 13194139534561 true] [17592186064112 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295521 13194139534561 true] [17592186064113 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295448 13194139534561 true] [17592186064113 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295452 13194139534561 true] [17592186064113 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295456 131941