{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.5) & =⌊3(0.5)+2⌋+2 \\\\  & =⌊1.5+2⌋+2 \\\\  & =⌊3.5⌋+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊3.5⌋=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.5) & =⌊3.5⌋+2 \\\\  & =3+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295432 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295433 13194139534561 true] [17592186295432 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534561 true] [17592186295432 1041 "field-1" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295432 1104 #edb/ref 17592186295433 13194139534561 true] [17592186295432 1110 #uuid "d01329be-979f-589c-8dde-5aefe42cefd5" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295433 1034 "5" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295433 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534561 true] [17592186295433 1111 #uuid "e2b6a198-eeda-5869-b789-4db047d408d3" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295434 1017 #edb/ref 17592186295435 13194139534561 true] [17592186295434 1089 "q-182037" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295434 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534561 true] [17592186295434 1100 "$⌊-9.86⌋=${{field-1}}" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295434 1113 #uuid "90ade7e1-ff2b-56b2-a925-bd8858c175d1" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295434 1145 "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⌊-9.86⌋=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295436 13194139534561 true] [17592186295435 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534561 true] [17592186295435 1041 "field-1" 13194139534561 true] [17592186295435 1104 #edb/ref 17592186295436 13194139534561 true] [17592186295435 1110 #uuid "acf6649a-c157-50da-b9fe-aa1f87808dc0" 13194139